title: '? Where the hardest decision needs what two territories know, two proposals written apart and one decider beat one author asking questions.'
pid: bb270a35-8359-4b56-9b74-e7108c3d1a8f
body: |2-
  The rule is [[id:436d5e47-89df-41ab-b763-5f989994883e][the rule for when a second specialist joins a plan]].
  Val's and Terry's code is interleaved inside one function; Drew and
  Cleo share what a redraw sends. Trial: the next request whose
  hardest decision sits on one of those borders. Have both owners
  propose apart, then count what each proposal holds that the other
  lacks and the decision used. If the author's questions would plainly
  have reached all of it, drop the proposals and keep the questions.
